From e31f293e10edd61fb0266da7441ac080511143df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Md Sadre Alam <mdalam@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 11:30:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-msm: Fix ICE keyslot index for hardware key
 operations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When using hardware key slots with Inline Crypto Engine (ICE),
the driver was incorrectly passing software keyslot indices directly
to the hardware, causing timeout errors during dm-crypt operations.

The block crypto layer manages a pool of 32 software keyslots (indices 0-31)
for inline encryption. When dm-crypt creates encrypted device mappings,
it allocates keyslots sequentially:

1. blk_crypto_get_keyslot() is called for each new mapping
2. An idle slot is selected from the software keyslot pool
3. blk_crypto_keyslot_index() returns the slot index (0, 1, 2, 3...)
4. This index is stored in mrq->crypto_key_slot
5. The index is passed down to the MMC driver for hardware programming

For multiple dm-crypt mappings:
- First mapping  → software slot 0
- Second mapping → software slot 1
- Third mapping  → software slot 2
- And so on...

The Problem is Qualcomm ICE hardware has only 2 hardware keyslots
(indices 0-1) for hardware-wrapped keys managed by TEE/SCM. The block
crypto layer is unaware of this hardware limitation and continues allocating
software slots beyond index 1.

When the driver receives mrq->crypto_key_slot = 2 (or higher), it
attempts to program ICE hardware slot 2, which doesn't exist, causing:

  mmc0: Timeout waiting for hardware interrupt
  device-mapper: remove ioctl on test-crypt failed: Resource busy

The issue manifests when creating multiple dm-crypt mappings or when
keyslots are reused after eviction.

To Fix this add a check for cq_host->use_hwkey in sdhci_msm_ice_cfg().
When using hardware-wrapped keys, always force the keyslot index to 0,
regardless of the software slot index allocated by the block crypto layer.

This ensures that:
1. Software keyslot management continues normally in block crypto layer
2. Hardware operations always use valid ICE hardware slot 0
3. Multiple dm-crypt mappings work correctly with hardware keys

The software keyslot index is still used for key lookup and management
in the block crypto layer, but the hardware programming uses the fixed
hardware slot index.

Change-Id: I76d886efbca16056e7b8efd1d520438421e2775d
Signed-off-by: Md Sadre Alam <mdalam@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
index b15a80acaab0..c96fe30c1f3c 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-msm.c
@@ -1997,6 +1997,8 @@ static void sdhci_msm_ice_cfg(struct sdhci_host *host, struct mmc_request *mrq)
 		}
 
 		key_index = mrq->crypto_key_slot;
+		if (cq_host->use_hwkey)
+			key_index = 0;
 		crypto_params = FIELD_PREP(ICE_HCI_PARAM_CE, 1) |
 				FIELD_PREP(ICE_HCI_PARAM_CCI, key_index);
 
-- 
2.34.1

